>>On 15Jul1999 at 14:18, Serguei Chestopalov wrote:
>Nice project! Do you have a working version?

Yes.  These messages come directly from the 3c (via a modem).  It works but
is somewhat slow, hence why I want to rewrite some routines.  A couple of
the Tcp/Ip routines I wrote in assembler (FCS and Base64/UUcode) for speed.
It started as a "hack" project and it has evolved. I just recently removed
the hard coded stuff and put in a front end setup so that is a little more
user friendly.  I still have to write the code to strip off any attachments
in the incoming messages.

Mark



